Check CB011031 PM Data volume Counters
    [Documentation]   Compare data volume between Cell1 and Cell2

    Dated Log new line          ${trcColor}=== Compare DL data volume counters between CellId1 and CellId2 ${defColor}

    ${DlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell1}=    Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID
    ...                          ${LATEST_PM_FILE}         M55309C01001         1
    ${DlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell2}=    Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID
    ...                          ${LATEST_PM_FILE}         M55309C01001         2

    Dated Log new line          ${trcColor}=== Check if DLMacSDU volume counter of Cell1 ${DlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell1}
    ...                          is equal or above DLMacSDU volume counter of Cell2 ${DlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell2}   ${defColor}

    Should Be True      ${DlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell1} >= ${DlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell2}

    Dated Log new line          ${trcColor}=== Compare UL data volume counters between CellId1 and CellId2 ${defColor}

    ${UlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell1}=    Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID
    ...                          ${LATEST_PM_FILE}         M55309C02001         1
    ${UlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell2}=    Retrieve Latest Single Counter Value From Pm File with CellID
    ...                          ${LATEST_PM_FILE}         M55309C02001         2

    Dated Log new line          ${trcColor}=== Check if ULMacSDU volume counter of Cell1 ${UlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell1}
    ...                          is equal or above ULMacSDU volume counter of Cell2 ${UlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell2}   ${defColor}

    Should Be True      (${UlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell1}+(0.002*${UlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell1})) >= ${UlMacSDUVolDTCH_Cell2}
